1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,150
Contoso Hospitality. Group and events sales, with Cowork and Dynamics 365.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:10,665
Eight a.m. An RFP for a three-hundred-person sales kickoff lands in the group sales inbox.

3
00:00:10,665 --> 00:00:17,400
An intake agent reads it and creates the opportunity in Dynamics 365 Sales, with the dates, room block and space.

4
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:20,938
Group sales manager Kevin Tran asks Cowork to build the proposal.

5
00:00:20,938 --> 00:00:26,777
Cowork checks space, weighs the group against expected demand, and drafts it from past events and pricing rules.

6
00:00:26,777 --> 00:00:28,810
He reviews it and sends it before nine.

7
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:33,054
That afternoon, Kevin walks the ballroom with the planner, Denise Carter.

8
00:00:33,054 --> 00:00:37,820
She signs, and the contract, deposit and attrition terms are tracked in Dynamics 365.

9
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:39,652
Event week, the changes fly.

10
00:00:39,652 --> 00:00:45,720
Events manager Rosa Alvarez keeps every update in one place, and Cowork tells each team what changed.

11
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:54,430
At checkout, Cowork lines up the master bill in Dynamics 365 Finance against every event order, and flags two differences before Denise ever sees them.

12
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:57,405
From RFP to cash, without weeks of back and forth.

13
00:00:57,405 --> 00:01:01,868
Dynamics runs the deal, agents do the intake, and Cowork helps the team decide.

